# This file is generated by mstar
# the output contains inverse conductivity eff. masses
# m0/m_c = 1/3*Tr(m0/m*_ij) that
# are grouped by k-point index and then by the band index
# Each band record also gives the ID of its degenerate block (numbered
# from 1 at each k-point). Bands with the same block ID were treated
# together by degenerate perturbation theory (Eqs. 6 and 7 of the
# reference); adjacent bands belong to one block when their energies
# differ by no more than the degeneracy tolerance.
# A block is marked "# non-commuting block" when the effective matrices
# of its tensor components (Eq. 6) do not share eigenvectors (band
# warping). Each component is diagonalized separately and its eigenvalues
# are listed in ascending order, so a record then combines values that
# belong to different states [Phys. Rev. B 93, 205147 (2016), Sec. III].
# The values in such blocks are not defined for individual bands.
# columns correspond to
# band block m0/m_c
# KP: 1 NBCDER: 0 NEMAX: 428
# KP: 2 NBCDER: 3 NEMAX: 428
1 1  3.325948E-001
2 2  2.999588E-001
3 3  3.846557E-001
